  "The player area never got a size, so playback was not started.": "Taya' medidå-ña i player area, pot enao ti ha tutuhon i play.",
  "The player itself — decoding, subtitles and audio. GPLv2 or later.": "I player maisa — decoding, subtitulu yan audio. GPLv2 pat mås nuebu.",
  "The project does not host, run, endorse or recommend any source, and does not distribute a list of them.": "Este na proyekto ti ha host, ti ha maneha, ti ha aprueba yan ti ha rekomenda ni un source, ya ti ha nå'i lista siha.",
  "The release carries no update for this platform.": "Taya' update para este na plataforma gi este na release.",
  "The source fetched this already — it plays at once and keeps nothing on this device": "Ha chule' esta i source — ha play enseguidas ya taya' ha adahi gi este na device",
  "The torrent engine accepted the magnet but gave it no id.": "Ha aksepta i torrent engine i magnet lao taya' id ha nå'i.",
  "The torrent engine, embedded in the app. MIT licensed.": "I torrent engine, gaige gi sanhalom i app. MIT na lisensia.",
  "The torrent stream isn't ready yet (engine replied HTTP {status}). It may still be fetching metadata from peers.": "Trå'i listo i torrent stream (i engine manoppe HTTP {status}). Siña ha kokonne' trabia metadata ginen i peers.",
  "The update couldn't be installed: {error}": "Ti siña ma instala i update: {error}",
  "Theme": "Tema",
  "There is barely room for one film here. Plug a USB drive into the box — formatted FAT32, which every Android box accepts — and it appears above to download onto instead.": "Ti sen meggai espasio guini para un peliku'la ha'. Pega un USB drive gi box — format komo FAT32, ni ha aksepta kada Android box — ya u annok gi sanhilo' para un na'tunok guihi.",
  "There is no account to sign in to and nothing syncs to a server. What you watch, how far you got, your favourites and your watchlist are all stored on this device and never leave it. Syncing between screens is planned; until then, the backup below is how a library moves.": "Taya' kuenta para un sign in ya taya' ma sync para un server. Håfa un e'egga', asta månu måtto hao, i favorite-mu yan i watchlist-mu todu ma adahi gi este na device ya taya' nai humånao. Ma plåplanea i sync entre screen; asta ayu, i backup gi sanpapa' i chalan para un mudi i library.",
  "There's no {file} in your documents folder. Copy one there and try again.": "Taya' {file} gi folder dokumento-mu. Kopia uno guihi ya chagi ta'lo.",
  "This connection is metered right now.": "Metered este na koneksion på'go.",
  "This connection is not metered right now.": "Ti metered este na koneksion på'go.",
  "This copy wasn't installed by Rivulet's own installer — a package manager, or a build from source — so whatever put it there is what updates it. Replacing the files from in here would only confuse it.": "TODO_TRANSLATION: This copy wasn't installed by Rivulet's own installer — a package manager, or a build from source — so whatever put it there is what updates it. Replacing the files from in here would only confuse it.",
  "This device's decoder gave up on the file. That is usually the audio: Dolby (AC-3, E-AC-3, TrueHD) and DTS are not licensed into the system webview, so a release carrying one plays as a picture with no sound, or not at all. An x264 release with AAC audio will play.": "Ha dingu i decoder este na device i fail. Meggai na biåhi i audio: Dolby (AC-3, E-AC-3, TrueHD) yan DTS ti manlisensiadu gi system webview, pot enao un release yan uno siha ha play komo litratu ha' taya' sonido, pat ti ha play. Un x264 na release yan AAC na audio siña ha play.",
  "This file has one audio track.": "Un track audio ha' guaha gi este na fail.",
  "This is separate from the performance switch below on purpose. That one turns off blur, which is expensive to draw; the movement here is built out of the two things a graphics chip does almost for free, so a television can usually keep it.": "TODO_TRANSLATION: This is separate from the performance switch below on purpose. That one turns off blur, which is expensive to draw; the movement here is built out of the two things a graphics chip does almost for free, so a television can usually keep it.",
